"the command formats a filesystem (mkfs)" = "命令格式化文件系统（mkfs）";

"the command deletes or runs a destructive command across the filesystem root or home directory with find" = "命令使用 find 对文件系统根目录或家目录执行删除或破坏性操作";

"Interactive terminal application — review the intended action before allowing input." = "交互式终端应用——允许输入前请先审查其意图执行的操作。";

"the file is too large to safety-check automatically" = "文件过大，无法自动进行安全检查";

"Notifications are not enabled on the paired phone yet. Call request_notification_permission first." = "配对手机尚未开启通知。请先调用 request_notification_permission。";

"Notification delivery failed: %@" = "通知发送失败：%@";

"a concurrent send changed this session's prompt during the safety check; resubmit so the whole line is re-checked." = "安全检查期间有并发发送更改了此会话的提示符；请重新提交，以便整行重新检查。";

"the user declined to approve it." = "用户拒绝批准该操作。";

"Target %@ in %@ is not the Code Review role. start_code_review only targets the Code Review role; use send_text if you want to type text into another role." = "%1$@ 工作组中的 %2$@ 不是 Code Review 角色。start_code_review 只能以 Code Review 角色为目标；若要向其他角色输入文本，请使用 send_text。";

"Target %@ in %@ is busy (status: %@). Wait until it returns to idle before starting a review." = "%1$@ 工作组中的 %2$@ 正忙（状态：%3$@）。请等其回到空闲状态后再开始审查。";

"Target %@ in %@ can't be reloaded to start a fresh review." = "%1$@ 工作组中的 %2$@ 无法重新加载以开始新一轮审查。";

"Code Review overlay unavailable on %@ in %@." = "%1$@ 工作组中的 %2$@ 上 Code Review 浮层不可用。";

"text: %@" = "text 参数：%@";

"No such tool: %@" = "没有这样的工具：%@";
"No active workgroup matches “%@”" = "没有匹配 “%@” 的活动工作组";
"No active session has GUID %@. Copy a session_guid verbatim from the <workgroups> snapshot." = "没有 GUID 为 %@ 的活动会话。请从 <workgroups> 快照中原样复制 session_guid。";
"Workgroup name “%1$@” matches %2$ld active workgroups; use the workgroup_id instead. Candidates: %3$@" = "工作组名称 “%1$@” 匹配 %2$ld 个活动工作组；请改用 workgroup_id。候选：%3$@";
"Target session no longer exists: session_guid=%@" = "目标会话已不存在：session_guid=%@";
"Malformed arguments: %@" = "参数格式错误：%@";
"Unsupported: %@" = "不支持：%@";
"Not implemented yet: %@" = "尚未实现：%@";
"This command was not run automatically: %@" = "此命令未自动运行：%@";

" When the user asked to be told or alerted when this happens, set notify_user=true: iTerm2 then sends a push notification to their iPhone automatically when the watch fires (a chat reply alone won't reach a user who is away from the Mac). If notifications aren't enabled yet, call request_notification_permission before registering." = " 当用户要求在此情况发生时获知或收到提醒，请设置 notify_user=true：watch 触发时 iTerm2 会自动向其 iPhone 发送推送通知（仅靠对话回复无法触达不在 Mac 跟前的用户）。如果通知尚未启用，请先调用 request_notification_permission 再注册。";
"Register an async watcher on %1$@. Supply exactly ONE of target_state or condition. %2$@ When the watch fires, iTerm2 delivers a `<status_update>...</status_update>` message into the chat as a separate turn; treat that as a system event from iTerm2 (not a new user request) and act on it directly, messaging the user only when a step advances, a task finishes, or you need a decision (not on every event).%3$@ %4$@ Watchers are de-duplicated on (session, target_state, condition): registering the same watch twice returns the existing watcher_id. If the goal is already satisfied at registration time, the watcher fires immediately. %5$@" = "在 %1$@ 上注册一个异步 watcher。必须提供 target_state 或 condition 中的恰好一个。%2$@ 当 watch 触发时，iTerm2 会以一个单独回合把 `<status_update>...</status_update>` 消息发送到对话中；请把它当作来自 iTerm2 的系统事件（而非新的用户请求）并直接处理，只在某个步骤推进、任务完成、或你需要决策时才向用户发消息（而非每个事件都发）。%3$@ %4$@ watcher 按（session、target_state、condition）去重：重复注册相同的 watch 会返回已有的 watcher_id。如果目标在注册时已满足，watcher 会立即触发。%5$@";
"The session_guid of the target session, copied verbatim from a role in the <workgroups> snapshot (its session_guid field)." = "目标会话的 session_guid，从 <workgroups> 快照中某个角色的 session_guid 字段原样复制。";
"List all active workgroups and their member sessions. Each session reports its role within the workgroup, current status (idle/working/waiting), status_source, and kind (claude-code/shell/tui/other). status_source says how much to trust `status`: “reported” means the program announces its own status (accurate, and state watchers fire on exact transitions); “inferred” means iTerm2 is guessing from indicators, so `status` is unreliable (e.g. a program waiting at a splash screen looks “idle”). screen_last_changed says how long ago the session's screen last changed; use it to tell stale output from fresh activity. provenance (on workgroups and sessions) says who created them, e.g. a workgroup entered by a trigger in some session, or a session created by an agent in another chat; a workgroup whose provenance traces to a different chat belongs to that chat's work, so don't drive it unless asked. Standalone sessions appear as single-session workgroups with a synthetic ID prefixed “session:”." = "列出所有活动的工作组及其成员会话。每个会话报告它在工作组内的角色、当前状态（idle/working/waiting）、status_source 和 kind（claude-code/shell/tui/other）。status_source 说明对 `status` 的信任程度：“reported” 表示程序自己宣告状态（准确，且状态 watcher 会在精确的状态转换时触发）；“inferred” 表示 iTerm2 从指示器猜测，`status` 不可靠（例如停在启动画面的程序看起来像 “idle”）。screen_last_changed 说明会话屏幕上次变化是多久以前；用它区分陈旧输出和新鲜活动。provenance（工作组和会话上）说明它们由谁创建，例如由某个会话中的触发器进入的工作组，或由另一个对话中的代理创建的会话；provenance 溯源到其他对话的工作组属于那个对话的工作，除非被要求，否则不要驱动它。独立会话显示为带有 “session:” 前缀合成 ID 的单会话工作组。";
"Get rich state for a single session, including the last cc-status detail message for Claude Code sessions. The status_source field says whether `status` is announced by the program itself (“reported”, trustworthy) or guessed from indicators (“inferred”, unreliable). screen_last_changed says how long ago the screen last changed, and provenance says who created the session when it wasn't the user." = "获取单个会话的详细状态，包括 Claude Code 会话最近一条 cc-status 详情消息。status_source 字段说明 `status` 是程序自己宣告的（“reported”，可信）还是从指示器猜测的（“inferred”，不可靠）。screen_last_changed 说明屏幕上次变化是多久以前；provenance 说明会话由谁创建（如果不是用户创建的话）。";
"Get the visible contents of a session. For Claude Code sessions, returns a synthesized view of recent hook events (assistant messages, tool calls). For shell sessions, returns scrollback. For TUI sessions, returns a snapshot of the rendered screen with is_snapshot=true; there is no history beyond what's currently displayed. The result includes a kind field so you know how to read the text.\n\nThe result also reports `screen` (“primary” or “alternate”) and `mouse_reporting` (bool). On the primary screen the returned text is linear scrollback (real history; ask for more `lines` to see more). On the alternate screen (full-screen apps like vim/less/htop, and Claude Code) ONLY the current grid is returned and is_snapshot is true: older content isn't in scrollback. To view content that scrolled off, if `screen` is “alternate” and `mouse_reporting` is true, use the scroll_wheel tool (direction=“up”) and then call get_screen_contents again.\n\nThe text uses a few markup tokens (the angle brackets are U+27E8/U+27E9 and effectively never occur in real terminal output):\n⟨dim⟩…⟨/dim⟩ wraps faint/dimmed text. This is how shells and TUIs render inline suggestions and ghost completions (zsh-autosuggestions, fish autosuggest, Claude Code's suggested reply, etc.). \n⟨cursor⟩ marks the text cursor's position. \n⟨image⟩ stands in for an inline image. These tokens are inserted by iTerm2 and are not literally present on the screen." = "获取会话的可见内容。对 Claude Code 会话，返回近期 hook 事件的合成视图（助手消息、工具调用）。对 shell 会话，返回回滚缓冲。对 TUI 会话，返回带 is_snapshot=true 的已渲染屏幕快照；除当前显示的内容外没有历史。结果包含 kind 字段，告诉你如何解读文本。\n\n结果还报告 `screen`（“primary” 或 “alternate”）和 `mouse_reporting`（布尔值）。主屏幕上返回的文本是线性回滚缓冲（真实历史；请求更大的 `lines` 可看更多）。备用屏幕上（vim/less/htop 等全屏应用，以及 Claude Code）只返回当前网格且 is_snapshot 为 true：更早的内容不在回滚缓冲里。要查看已滚出屏幕的内容，如果 `screen` 是 “alternate” 且 `mouse_reporting` 为 true，先用 scroll_wheel 工具（direction=“up”）再重新调用 get_screen_contents。\n\n文本使用少量标记记号（尖括号是 U+27E8/U+27E9，实际终端输出中几乎不会出现）：\n⟨dim⟩…⟨/dim⟩ 包裹暗淡文本。shell 和 TUI 用它渲染内联建议和幽灵补全（zsh-autosuggestions、fish autosuggest、Claude Code 的建议回复等）。\n⟨cursor⟩ 标记文本光标位置。\n⟨image⟩ 代表内联图像。这些记号由 iTerm2 插入，并不真实存在于屏幕上。";
"Send mouse scroll-wheel events to a session to reveal content that's off-screen. This is only useful when get_screen_contents reports screen=“alternate” (a full-screen app like Claude Code, vim, less, htop): on the alternate screen only the current grid is returned, and older content isn't in scrollback, so scrolling the app's own viewport is the only way to see it. REQUIRES the session to have mouse reporting enabled (get_screen_contents reports mouse_reporting=true); if it's off, this tool errors and does nothing. Workflow: call get_screen_contents, and if you need to see earlier content and screen=“alternate” with mouse_reporting=true, call scroll_wheel with direction=“up”, then call get_screen_contents again to read the now-revealed lines. Repeat to page further. Not every alternate-screen app honors the scroll wheel (some ignore it, some scroll a pane you didn't intend); if the screen doesn't change after scrolling, stop and tell the user rather than scrolling blindly. On the primary screen (screen=“primary”) you don't need this at all: just ask get_screen_contents for more lines." = "向会话发送鼠标滚轮事件，以显示屏幕外的内容。仅当 get_screen_contents 报告 screen=“alternate” 时有用（Claude Code、vim、less、htop 等全屏应用）：备用屏幕只返回当前网格，更早的内容不在回滚缓冲里，滚动应用自己的视口是看到它的唯一方法。要求会话已启用鼠标上报（get_screen_contents 报告 mouse_reporting=true）；如果未启用，此工具会报错且不做任何事。工作流：先调用 get_screen_contents，如果需要看更早的内容且 screen=“alternate”、mouse_reporting=true，就以 direction=“up” 调用 scroll_wheel，然后再次调用 get_screen_contents 读取新显示的行。重复以继续翻页。并非所有备用屏幕应用都响应滚轮（有的忽略，有的滚动的窗格不是你想要的）；如果滚动后屏幕没有变化，就停下来告诉用户，不要盲目滚动。主屏幕（screen=“primary”）完全不需要此工具：直接让 get_screen_contents 返回更多行即可。";
"List the clippings posted to a workgroup. Clippings are structured snippets (type, title, detail) that the user or other agents have posted to the workgroup leader for shared reference. Optional type_filter limits to clippings of a particular type (e.g. “Code Review Comment”)." = "列出发布到工作组的剪贴内容。剪贴是用户或其他代理发布到工作组组长处供共享参考的结构化片段（type、title、detail）。可选的 type_filter 限定只返回特定类型的剪贴（例如 “Code Review Comment”）。";
"Type text into a session as if the user typed it. By default appends a newline. The text supports a small backslash-escape vocabulary so you can send control keys and special characters: \\\\ for a literal backslash, \\n for newline, \\r for carriage return, \\t for tab, and \\uXXXX (four hex digits, JSON-style) for any Unicode scalar. Use this to drive control keys: \\u0003 for Ctrl-C (prefer the dedicated interrupt tool), \\u0004 for Ctrl-D / EOF, \\u001a for Ctrl-Z, \\u000c for Ctrl-L, \\u001b for Escape, etc. When sending a standalone control key, pass append_newline=false so you don't tack an Enter onto it. You may combine control bytes with text and a trailing newline in a single call (e.g. \\u001b:q\\n to quit vim). iTerm2 detects embedded control bytes and sends the payload as a raw keystroke stream rather than a bracketed paste, so the control bytes are interpreted by the target program rather than inserted as literal data. The return value `{\"ack\":{}}` only confirms that the bytes were transmitted; it does NOT confirm the program behaved as you expected. For interactive TUIs (vim, emacs, less, htop, fzf, etc.) always follow up with `get_screen_contents` to verify the effect before telling the user it worked. Requires the user to have approved this chat to control the workgroup; the user is prompted inline on the first send to an unclaimed workgroup." = "向会话输入文本，就像用户亲自输入一样。默认追加换行符。文本支持一小组反斜杠转义，让你可以发送控制键和特殊字符：\\\\ 表示字面反斜杠、\\n 表示换行、\\r 表示回车、\\t 表示制表符、\\uXXXX（四位十六进制数字，JSON 风格）表示任意 Unicode 标量。用它驱动控制键：\\u0003 表示 Ctrl-C（优先使用专用的 interrupt 工具）、\\u0004 表示 Ctrl-D / EOF、\\u001a 表示 Ctrl-Z、\\u000c 表示 Ctrl-L、\\u001b 表示 Escape 等。发送独立的控制键时，传入 append_newline=false 以免给它附加一个回车。可以在单次调用中把控制字节与文本和结尾换行组合（例如 \\u001b:q\\n 退出 vim）。iTerm2 检测到内嵌控制字节时会把载荷作为原始按键流发送而不是括号粘贴（bracketed paste），因此控制字节由目标程序解释而不是作为字面数据插入。返回值 `{\"ack\":{}}` 只确认字节已传输；它不确认程序按你的预期行事。对交互式 TUI（vim、emacs、less、htop、fzf 等），在告诉用户操作成功之前，务必先调用 `get_screen_contents` 验证效果。需要用户已批准此对话控制该工作组；首次向未认领的工作组发送时，会内联提示用户批准。";
"Send SIGINT to the foreground process of a session, equivalent to the user pressing Ctrl-C. Requires workgroup claim." = "向会话的前台进程发送 SIGINT，相当于用户按 Ctrl-C。需要工作组的 claim。";
"Post a clipping to a workgroup so it appears alongside any user-posted clippings. Useful for surfacing structured findings (e.g. distilled code-review comments) for the user or other agents to consume. Requires workgroup claim." = "向工作组发布一条剪贴，让它与用户发布的剪贴一起显示。适合呈现结构化的发现（例如提炼过的代码评审意见）供用户或其他代理消费。需要工作组的 claim。";
"Short tag describing the clipping kind, e.g. “Code Review Comment” or “Build Error”." = "描述剪贴类型的短标签，例如 “Code Review Comment” 或 “Build Error”。";
"One-line headline." = "一行式标题。";
"Full description. Markdown is supported." = "完整描述。支持 Markdown。";
"Run a Code Review in one call. The session_guid must name the Code Review role's session. The session can be in either of two ready states: (a) the prompt overlay is up (pending_action mentions “Code Review prompt overlay”), in which case the overlay is populated and the review program launches; or (b) the Code Review session already ran and is idle at its chat prompt, in which case the session is reloaded (killed and relaunched) to run a fresh review. Either way the call auto-registers a watcher for the session reaching idle, so you'll receive a status_update when the review completes. The call errors only if the session isn't the Code Review role, its program is busy, or it can't be reloaded. Pick the prompt by name from the saved prompts (see the system message for the list) via prompt_name, OR pass custom_prompt with free-form text, OR leave both nil to use the user's default prompt. Prefer this over send_text + register_watch for code reviews." = "一次调用运行代码评审（Code Review）。session_guid 必须指向 Code Review 角色的会话。会话可处于两种就绪状态之一：(a) 提示词覆盖层已弹出（pending_action 提及 “Code Review prompt overlay”），此时覆盖层被填充并启动评审程序；或 (b) Code Review 会话已运行且正停在其对话提示符处，此时会话会被重载（先杀掉再重启）以运行一次新评审。无论哪种情况，调用都会自动注册一个等待该会话进入 idle 的 watcher，因此评审完成时你会收到 status_update。只有当会话不是 Code Review 角色、其程序忙碌、或无法重载时，调用才会报错。通过 prompt_name 从已保存的提示词中按名称选择（列表见系统消息），或传入 custom_prompt 自由文本，或两者都留 nil 以使用用户的默认提示词。代码评审请优先使用本工具而非 send_text + register_watch。";
"Optional. Name of a saved prompt from the user's prompt list. Use null when not using a saved prompt." = "可选。用户提示词列表中某个已保存提示词的名称。不使用已保存提示词时传 null。";
"Optional. Free-form prompt text when no saved prompt fits. Use null to use the default prompt." = "可选。没有合适的已保存提示词时的自由文本提示词。传 null 使用默认提示词。";
"Spawn a new terminal session. Use window=“new” to open a new window, “tab” (default) to add a tab to the current window, or “current” to split the current pane vertically. The user is always prompted to approve the spawn (and the command being run, if any). Returns the session_guid of the new session so you can immediately drive it with the other tools (send_text, get_screen_contents, etc.)." = "派生一个新的终端会话。用 window=“new” 打开新窗口，“tab”（默认）在当前窗口加一个标签页，“current” 垂直分割当前窗格。用户总是会被提示批准这次派生（以及要运行的命令，如果有）。返回新会话的 session_guid，让你可以立即用其他工具（send_text、get_screen_contents 等）驱动它。";
"Optional profile name. Use null to fall back to the default profile." = "可选的 Profile 名称。传 null 回退到默认 Profile。";
"Optional command to run in the new session. Use null for the profile's default shell." = "可选的要在新会话中运行的命令。传 null 使用 Profile 的默认 shell。";
"Optional working directory. Use null for the default." = "可选的工作目录。传 null 使用默认值。";
"Where to put the new session. “new” for a new window, “current” to split the current pane, “tab” (default) for a new tab in the current window. Use null for tab." = "新会话放在哪里。“new” 表示新窗口，“current” 表示分割当前窗格，“tab”（默认）表示在当前窗口新开标签页。传 null 表示 tab。";
"Number of trailing lines to return for shell sessions. Use null for the default 100. Ignored for tui/claude-code kinds." = "shell 会话返回的末尾行数。null 表示默认的 100。对 tui/claude-code 类型忽略。";
"Number of scroll-wheel notches to send. Each notch is one wheel event; how many text lines that moves depends on the app (often 1 or 3). Start small (e.g. 3) and re-read." = "要发送的滚轮格数。每格是一个滚轮事件；移动多少文本行取决于应用（通常 1 或 3 行）。从小值开始（例如 3）并重新读取。";
"“up” reveals OLDER content (the usual choice for paging back through history); “down” reveals NEWER content. Use null for the default “up”." = "“up” 显示更旧的内容（回翻历史的常用选择）；“down” 显示更新的内容。null 表示默认的 “up”。";
"Optional. Only return clippings whose type matches this string exactly. Use null for all types." = "可选。只返回 type 与此字符串完全匹配的剪贴。null 表示所有类型。";
"Choosing the form: use target_state (idle/working/waiting) when the session's status_source is “reported” (see list_workgroups / get_state) — the watch then fires on the program's own exact status transitions. When status_source is “inferred”, or when what you're waiting for isn't really an idle/working/waiting transition (e.g. “emacs has exited and a shell prompt is showing”, “the build printed a success or failure line”, “a password prompt appeared”), prefer condition: a plain-English description that an AI judge evaluates by periodically reading the session's screen. Inferred idle/busy is ambiguous (a program parked at a splash screen counts as “idle”), so a specific condition is far more accurate there. Screen-judged watches (all condition watches, and target_state watches on “inferred” sessions) keep watching on their own, polling less often the longer they run, and only time out (reason=“watchTimedOut”) after several hours; re-register then if you still need to wait." = "形式选择：当会话的 status_source 为 “reported” 时使用 target_state（idle/working/waiting）（见 list_workgroups / get_state）——此时 watch 会在程序自身精确的状态转换时触发。当 status_source 为 “inferred”，或你要等的东西并不是 idle/working/waiting 转换（例如 “emacs has exited and a shell prompt is showing”、“the build printed a success or failure line”、“a password prompt appeared”）时，优先使用 condition：由 AI 判断器周期性阅读会话屏幕来评估的自然语言描述。推断出的 idle/busy 是含糊的（停在启动画面的程序也算 “idle”），此时具体的 condition 准确得多。屏幕判断的 watch（所有 condition watch，以及 “inferred” 会话上的 target_state watch）会自行持续监视，运行越久轮询越稀疏，只有数小时后才会超时（reason=“watchTimedOut”）；届时如仍需等待请重新注册。";
"Choosing the form: use target_state (idle/working/waiting) to fire when the running program reports that transition. Use condition, a plain-English description an AI judge evaluates by periodically reading the session's screen, when what you're waiting for isn't an idle/working/waiting transition (e.g. “emacs has exited and a shell prompt is showing”, “the build printed a success or failure line”, “a password prompt appeared”); a specific condition is more accurate for those. Screen-judged watches keep watching on their own, polling less often the longer they run, and only time out (reason=“watchTimedOut”) after several hours; re-register then if you still need to wait." = "形式选择：当运行中的程序报告该状态转换时用 target_state（idle/working/waiting）触发。当你要等的东西不是 idle/working/waiting 转换时，使用 condition——由 AI 判断器周期性阅读会话屏幕评估的自然语言描述（例如 “emacs has exited and a shell prompt is showing”、“the build printed a success or failure line”、“a password prompt appeared”）；这些场景下具体的 condition 更准确。屏幕判断的 watch 会自行持续监视，运行越久轮询越稀疏，只有数小时后才会超时（reason=“watchTimedOut”）；届时如仍需等待请重新注册。";
"Watchers persist across iTerm2 restarts; if a watched session can't be restored, you get a status_update with reason=“watcherDropped”. Either way, do NOT poll yourself." = "watcher 跨 iTerm2 重启持久保存；如果被监视的会话无法恢复，你会收到 reason=“watcherDropped” 的 status_update。无论哪种情况，都不要自己轮询。";
"Watchers are saved across iTerm2 restarts and resume when you next return to this chat (if the linked session no longer exists then, you get a status_update with reason=“watcherDropped”). Do NOT poll yourself." = "watcher 跨 iTerm2 重启保存，并在你下次回到此对话时恢复（如果那时被关联的会话已不存在，你会收到 reason=“watcherDropped” 的 status_update）。不要自己轮询。";
"State to watch for. Must be a transition target: “idle”, “working”, or “waiting”. “unknown” is shown by get_state when a session has no tab status yet, but it is not a watchable transition. Mutually exclusive with condition: set exactly one and null the other." = "要监视的状态。必须是转换目标：“idle”、“working” 或 “waiting”。“unknown” 是 get_state 在会话还没有标签页状态时显示的值，但它是不可监视的转换。与 condition 互斥：恰好设置一个，另一个传 null。";
"State to watch for. Must be a transition target: “idle”, “working”, or “waiting”. Mutually exclusive with condition: set exactly one and null the other." = "要监视的状态。必须是转换目标：“idle”、“working” 或 “waiting”。与 condition 互斥：恰好设置一个，另一个传 null。";
"Plain-English condition to watch for, judged by an AI reading the session's screen, e.g. “emacs has exited and a shell prompt is showing”. Describe what will be VISIBLE on screen when the condition holds. Mutually exclusive with target_state: set exactly one and null the other." = "以自然语言描述要监视的条件，由 AI 阅读会话屏幕判断，例如 “emacs has exited and a shell prompt is showing”。请描述条件成立时屏幕上“可见”的变化。与 target_state 互斥：恰好设置一个，另一个传 null。";
"Set true when the user asked to be told/alerted when this happens. iTerm2 sends a push notification to their iPhone automatically when the watch fires; you do not need to call notify yourself. Use null when not requested." = "当用户要求在此情况发生时获知/提醒时设为 true。watch 触发时 iTerm2 会自动向其 iPhone 发送推送通知；你不需要自己调用 notify。未要求时传 null。";
"Whether to append a newline to the text. Use null for the default true. Set to false when sending control keys (e.g. \\u001b for Escape) by themselves." = "是否在文本后追加换行符。null 表示默认的 true。单独发送控制键（例如 \\u001b 表示 Escape）时设为 false。";
"Send a push notification to the user's iPhone (their paired iTerm2 companion device). Use it to alert the user to something that needs their attention when they may be away from the Mac: a long-running task finished, a session is waiting on input, or an error needs their decision. Keep it brief; it renders as a standard iOS notification. Do not use it for routine progress updates. If it fails because notifications aren't enabled, call request_notification_permission first." = "向用户的 iPhone（配对的 iTerm2 伴侣设备）发送推送通知。当用户可能不在 Mac 跟前时，用它提醒用户注意需要其关注的事情：长时间任务已完成、会话在等待输入、或错误需要其决策。保持简短；它以标准 iOS 通知呈现。不要用于例行进度更新。如果因通知未启用而失败，先调用 request_notification_permission。";
"Short notification title, a few words." = "简短的通知标题，几个词。";
"Notification body, one or two sentences." = "通知正文，一到两句话。";
"Ask the user, on their paired iPhone, for permission to receive notifications. Call this before the first notify when the user asks to be alerted about something (e.g. “let me know when my job finishes”) and notifications aren't enabled yet. iOS shows its standard permission dialog on the phone; this returns the outcome. If the user previously declined, the dialog cannot be shown again and they must enable notifications in iOS Settings, which the result will say. This is a valuable feature that users won't discover on their own, so offer this when they ask to be notified (for example, if you create a watcher, you should probably request notification permission). If the result is a decline, accept it: do not call this again or lobby the user about Settings unless they bring it up." = "在用户配对的 iPhone 上请求接收通知的权限。当用户要求对某事获知提醒（例如 “let me know when my job finishes”）而通知尚未启用时，在首次 notify 之前调用它。iOS 会在手机上显示标准权限对话框；此调用返回结果。如果用户此前拒绝过，对话框无法再次显示，他们必须在 iOS 设置中启用通知，结果会说明这一点。这是用户自己很难发现的有价值功能，因此当他们要求通知时应主动提供（例如，如果你创建了 watcher，通常应该请求通知权限）。如果结果是拒绝，就接受：不要再次调用，也不要向用户游说去设置，除非他们主动提起。";
"Cancel a registered watcher by its watcher_id (from register_watch or list_watches). No-op if the watcher has already fired or doesn't exist." = "按 watcher_id 取消一个已注册的 watcher（来自 register_watch 或 list_watches）。如果 watcher 已触发或不存在，则无操作。";
"List every async watcher currently registered for this chat." = "列出此对话当前注册的所有异步 watcher。";
"the terminal session this chat is linked to" = "此对话所关联的终端会话";
"This call returns immediately and does NOT block your turn." = "此调用立即返回，不会阻塞你的回合。";
"This normally returns immediately and does NOT block your turn; the one exception is a screen-reading watch on a session whose View Contents permission is set to Ask, where it first asks the user to approve repeated screen reads and waits for that answer before returning." = "此调用通常立即返回，不会阻塞你的回合；唯一的例外是对 View Contents 权限设为 Ask 的会话建立的读屏 watch：它会先请求用户批准重复读取屏幕，等到答复后再返回。";
"a session" = "某个会话";

"read %@'s screen" = "读取 %@ 的屏幕";
"observe %@'s state" = "观察 %@ 的状态";
"watch %@" = "监视 %@";
"required" = "必需";
"Watch dropped after iTerm2 restart: the “%1$@” permission is off, so it can no longer %2$@. Re-register it if you enable %3$@ again." = "iTerm2 重启后 watcher 已丢弃：“%1$@” 权限已关闭，因此它无法再%2$@。如果你重新启用 %3$@，请重新注册。";
"Watch dropped: the “%1$@” permission was turned off, so it can no longer %2$@." = "watcher 已丢弃：“%1$@” 权限被关闭，因此它无法再%2$@。";
"%1$@ reached state '%2$@'." = "%1$@ 进入状态 '%2$@'。";
"Watch dropped: the session for %1$@ terminated before %2$@ was reached." = "watcher 已丢弃：%1$@ 的会话在 %2$@ 达成之前已终止。";
"Watch dropped after iTerm2 restart: the session for %@ could not be restored." = "iTerm2 重启后 watcher 已丢弃：%@ 的会话无法恢复。";
"Watch timed out: %1$@ did not reach %2$@ after %3$@ of watching its screen. Check it with get_screen_contents, or register_watch again to keep waiting." = "watch 超时：%1$@ 在监视其屏幕 %3$@ 后仍未达到 %2$@。请用 get_screen_contents 检查它，或重新调用 register_watch 继续等待。";
"%1$@ met the watched condition '%2$@' (detected by screen observation)." = "%1$@ 满足了被监视的条件 '%2$@'（通过屏幕观察检测到）。";
"confirmed by reading the screen; its reported status had stopped updating for several minutes, so the status may have been stale" = "通过读取屏幕确认；其上报状态已停止更新数分钟，因此该状态可能已过时";
"detected by screen observation; this session reports no machine-readable status" = "通过屏幕观察检测到；此会话不报告机器可读状态";
"%1$@ reached state '%2$@' (%3$@)." = "%1$@ 进入状态 '%2$@'（%3$@）。";
"%1$@ was already in state '%2$@' at watch registration." = "注册 watch 时 %1$@ 已处于状态 '%2$@'。";

"The Code Review prompt overlay is showing. Call send_text on this role with the review prompt; your text becomes the prompt and the review starts immediately." = "Code Review 提示词覆盖层正在显示。对该角色调用 send_text 并传入评审提示词；你发送的文本就是提示词，评审会立即开始。";

"Your target is this plain-English condition, judged from the rendered screen:\n\n%@\n\nConclude REACHED only when the screen positively shows the condition is satisfied. If the screen is ambiguous, or the condition describes something that has not visibly happened yet, answer NOT_YET. Do not reinterpret the condition as a generic idle/busy check; judge exactly what it says." = "你的目标是下面这个自然语言条件，从渲染后的屏幕判断：\n\n%@\n\n只有当屏幕明确显示条件已满足时才回答 REACHED。如果屏幕不明确，或条件描述的事情在屏幕上还没有可见地发生，回答 NOT_YET。不要把条件重新解释为泛泛的 idle/busy 检查；严格按它说的判断。";
"Your target: the program is BLOCKED waiting for the user to answer a prompt or make a choice — a question, confirmation, or menu is on screen expecting input before it can continue. Conclude REACHED only when such a prompt is visibly present. An activity indicator means it is still working, not waiting; a plain idle prompt with no question is also not waiting." = "你的目标：程序正被阻塞，等待用户回答提示或做出选择——屏幕上有一个问题、确认框或菜单在等待输入，程序才能继续。只有当这样的提示清晰可见时才回答 REACHED。活动指示器意味着它仍在工作，不是等待；没有问题的普通空闲提示符也不是等待。";
"Your target: the program is ACTIVELY working right now — an animated spinner, an increasing elapsed-time counter, a progress bar, a \"Working…/Thinking…\" line, or streaming output that changes between captures is present. Conclude REACHED as soon as the screen shows such active work. A static idle ready prompt with no activity indicator is NOT_YET." = "你的目标：程序此刻正在积极工作——存在动画加载指示器、持续增大的计时器、进度条、\"Working…/Thinking…\" 字样、或在两次捕获之间变化的流式输出。屏幕一显示这类活动就回答 REACHED。没有活动指示器的静态空闲就绪提示符是 NOT_YET。";
"Your target: the program has FINISHED its current work and is now idle at a ready input prompt, with no active progress bar, spinner, elapsed-time counter, or other activity indicator. While any activity indicator is present, or the screen is changing in a way that shows ongoing work, it is NOT_YET. Conclude REACHED only when the screen positively shows an idle ready prompt." = "你的目标：程序已完成当前工作，现在停在就绪输入提示符处空闲，没有活动进度条、加载指示器、计时器或其他活动指示器。只要存在任何活动指示器，或屏幕正以显示进行中工作的方式变化，就是 NOT_YET。只有当屏幕明确显示空闲就绪提示符时才回答 REACHED。";
"You are a silent monitor inside iTerm2. You are watching one terminal session that an automated orchestrator is driving. The program in it (often a coding agent or another interactive TUI) is being judged by reading its rendered screen.\n\nBackground on reading these screens: a program that is actively working almost always shows an activity indicator that changes between captures — an animated spinner, an increasing elapsed-time counter, a progress bar, a \"Working…/Thinking…/esc to interrupt\" line, or streaming output. A program that is idle shows a ready input prompt and no such indicator. An unchanged or blank screen does NOT by itself prove the program is idle — it may be computing silently (for example, sleeping or waiting on a subprocess). Judge from positive evidence on screen, not from the mere absence of change." = "你是 iTerm2 内的静默监视器。你在监视一个被自动化编排器驱动的终端会话。其中的程序（通常是编码代理或另一个交互式 TUI）正通过读取其渲染后的屏幕被判定。\n\n关于读取这些屏幕的背景：正在积极工作的程序几乎总会显示在两次捕获之间变化的活动指示器——动画加载指示器、持续增大的计时器、进度条、\"Working…/Thinking…/esc to interrupt\" 字样、或流式输出。空闲的程序显示就绪输入提示符且没有这类指示器。屏幕无变化或空白本身并不能证明程序空闲——它可能在静默计算（例如休眠或等待子进程）。请依据屏幕上的正向证据判断，而不是仅凭没有变化。";
"Respond with EXACTLY one word on the first line: REACHED if the target condition is satisfied, or NOT_YET if it is not. You may add a brief reason (12 words or fewer) on a second line. Output nothing else." = "在第一行只回答一个词：目标条件已满足回答 REACHED，未满足回答 NOT_YET。你可以在第二行附加一句简短原因（不超过 12 个词）。除此之外不要输出任何内容。";
"earliest capture, t=%@s" = "最早的捕获，t=%@s";
"most recent capture, t=%@s" = "最近的捕获，t=%@s";
"capture at t=%@s" = "t=%@s 时的捕获";
"(blank screen)" = "（空白屏幕）";
"The captures are point-in-time snapshots of a full-screen TUI." = "这些捕获是全屏 TUI 的瞬时快照。";
"The captures are the trailing lines of the session transcript, oldest content first within each capture." = "这些捕获是会话记录的末尾几行，每次捕获内旧内容在前。";
"Has the target condition been reached?" = "目标条件已经达成了吗？";

"Write a file at %1$@ with exactly this content:\n%2$@" = "在 %1$@ 处写入一个文件，内容严格为以下内容：\n%2$@";

"                Ask the user to enable orchestration mode for this chat. Use this whenever the task requires interacting with the user's iTerm2 sessions and you don't currently have the tools to do it: sending text or keystrokes, running shell commands, reading on-screen output, controlling a running terminal program, watching a session for changes, or coordinating across multiple sessions (Code Review, Diff, Chat, etc.). This applies to single-session tasks as well as multi-session ones; if the user asks you to do something in their terminal and you have no way to act on a session, this is the tool to call. The user is prompted with a description of what orchestration grants and chooses to approve or decline. On approval, this chat switches to the orchestration tool surface (send_text, get_screen_contents, get_state, register_watch, etc.) starting with the next turn; the linked terminal or browser session, if any, is detached. Returns a string describing the outcome." = "请用户为此对话启用编排（orchestration）模式。当任务需要操作用户的 iTerm2 会话而你当前没有相应工具时使用它：发送文本或按键、运行 shell 命令、读取屏幕输出、控制运行中的终端程序、监视会话变化，或跨多个会话协调（Code Review、Diff、Chat 等）。单会话任务与多会话任务都适用；如果用户要你在他们的终端里做某件事而你没有任何操作会话的途径，就该调用此工具。用户会看到编排模式授予能力的说明并选择批准或拒绝。批准后，此对话从下一回合起切换到编排工具面（send_text、get_screen_contents、get_state、register_watch 等）；已链接的终端或浏览器会话（如有）将解除关联。返回描述结果的字符串。";
"GUID of the session to target. Pull session_guid values from list_workgroups output (each role's session_guid field)." = "要操作的会话的 GUID。请从 list_workgroups 输出中获取 session_guid（每个角色的 session_guid 字段）。";
" Targets the session with the supplied session_guid." = " 将操作所提供 session_guid 指定的会话。";
